  ("Why it happens", "<p>These tendons tolerate load well but compression very badly. Crossing your legs, sleeping on your side with the top knee dropped or standing with your weight on one hip squashes them against the bone. If the gluteal muscles are also weak, the pelvis drops with every step and the compression is repeated thousands of times a day.</p>"),
